Better version for Red Hat, because nologin path may be either /sbin/nologin or /usr/sbin/nologin. This avoids dependency on which nologin:

#!/bin/bash
awk -F: '
$1 !~ /^(root|halt|sync|shutdown)$/ &&
$7 !~ /(nologin|false)$/ {
    print $1, $6
}
' /etc/passwd

So if you want, you can replace this part in all scripts:

grep -Ev '^(root|halt|sync|shutdown)' /etc/passwd | \
awk -F: '($7 != "'"$(which nologin)"'" && $7 != "/bin/false") { print $1, $6 }'

with this cleaner Red Hat compatible part:

